SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CST: GLEAM 2027: Request for Light-Based Artwork Pro
 posals (Olbrich Botanical Gardens\; honorariums USD 5\,000 to 30\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 06 Jan 2027 at 23:59 CST.\n\nGLEAM is an annual night-ti
 me light art exhibition across a 16-acre botanical garden and a 10\,000 sq
  ft tropical conservatory. The 2027 edition will show 9 to 11 temporary\, 
 large-scale\, light-based works that are immersive\, interactive or kineti
 c\; 3 to 5 interactive works are wanted\, and traditional object-based scu
 lpture is not considered.\n\nOrganisation: Olbrich Botanical Gardens (City
  of Madison Parks Division and Olbrich Botanical Society)\nLocation: Madis
 on\, Wisconsin\, USA. Open to local\, regional and international artists\;
  works can be installed by local preparators if the artist cannot travel.\
 nAward: All-inclusive honorarium of USD 5\,000 to 30\,000 per artwork\, co
 vering artist fee\, materials\, fabrication\, travel\, lodging\, install a
 nd maintenance. Usually only one USD 30\,000 project is selected\; proposa
 ls under USD 25\,000 get the most consideration. Free host lodging and loa
 n projectors and speakers are available. No application fee stated.\nDurat
 ion: Install 4 to 24 August 2027\; exhibition 28 August to 23 October 2027
 \; de-install late October to early November 2027\n\nMore: https://www.olb
 richgleam.org/submit-a-proposal?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.olbrichgleam.org/submit-a-proposal?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Madison\, Wisconsin\, USA. Open to local\, regional and internatio
 nal artists\; works can be installed by local preparators if the artist ca
 nnot travel.
END:VEVENT
